  <main><article class="article wrap"><p class="eyebrow">FESTIVALS · 26 JULY 2026</p><h1>Guru Purnima 2026: a day to honour learning, guidance and gratitude</h1><p class="lead">Guru Purnima falls on Wednesday, 29 July 2026. For many of us, it is a beautiful pause to remember the teachers, elders and experiences that have shaped our path.</p><img class="hero-image" src="/images/deepak-maheshwari-yellow.png" alt="Deepak Maheshwari of Click Jyotish" />
  <h2>Why Guru Purnima matters</h2><p>Guru Purnima is observed on Ashadha Purnima and is also known as Vyasa Purnima. The day is traditionally connected with Maharshi Veda Vyasa and with the larger idea of the guru: someone who helps turn confusion into understanding. A guru may be a spiritual teacher, parent, mentor, book, or even a difficult life lesson that brings maturity.</p>
  <h2>2026 date for New Delhi</h2><p>In New Delhi, Purnima Tithi begins at 6:21 pm on 28 July and ends at 8:07 pm on 29 July. The observance day is Wednesday, 29 July. For a personal puja or any time-sensitive practice, always confirm the relevant local panchang and follow your family tradition.</p>
  <h2>A simple, sincere way to observe</h2><ol><li>Begin the day with a calm bath and a few minutes of silence.</li><li>Offer a prayer, flowers or simply heartfelt gratitude to your chosen deity, guru or teacher.</li><li>Call or message a teacher, parent or mentor who has helped you.</li><li>Read one page from a meaningful text, or make a small commitment to learning.</li><li>Give dakshina, donate books, or help someone learn—according to your ability.</li></ol>
  <h2>A Jyotish perspective</h2><p>In Vedic tradition, Guru (Jupiter) represents wisdom, counsel, expansion and ethical understanding. Rather than treating the day as a shortcut for instant results, use it to strengthen your relationship with learning and right guidance. If you are considering study, a new mentor, marriage, career direction or spiritual discipline, write down your question clearly. That clarity itself is a useful beginning.</p>
